>> title: Mojo Marinade
>> category: Spice Blends & Marinades
>> tags: cuban, garlic, citrus, marinade, pork
>> counters: Taquería, Deli
>> aka: mojo, mojo criollo, mojo de ajo
>> pairs-with: cuban-black-beans
>> servings: 8
>> time: 20 min
>> step.1: mash to a paste in a mortar
>> step.2: work in
>> step.3: warm, pour over, sizzle 1 min
>> step.4: whisk in
>> step.5: stir in, rest 15 min

Mash @garlic{8%cloves} with @kosher salt{1%tsp} and @black peppercorns{1%tsp} to a paste in a #mortar{}.

Work @ground cumin{1%tsp} and @dried oregano{1%tsp} into @&(~1)garlic paste{}.

Warm @extra-virgin olive oil{1/2%cup}(120 mL) in a small #saucepan{} until it shimmers, pour it over @&(~1)paste{}, and let it sizzle ~{1%min}.

Whisk @sour orange juice{3/4%cup}(180 mL; or 1/2 cup orange juice plus 1/4 cup lime juice) into @&(~1)mojo{}.

Stir @yellow onion{1/2}(thinly sliced) into @&(~1)mojo{} and let it sit ~{15%min} before using.
